title: $:/lithic/styles/pyramid.css
tags: $:/tags/Stylesheet
type: text/css

/*
Pyramid sidebar ($:/lithic/ui/SideBar/Pyramid): converts the active nodestream
into a mermaid tree and marks the node mirroring the tiddler currently being
edited with the `activeStyle` class (see the macro's `:::activeStyle` hints).
The old hardcoded classDefs (fill:#444/#666/#aaa + grey linkStyle) were removed
so the whole tree inherits the Contrast-locked mermaid defaults - including
palette-derived arrowhead markers - and only the active node needs special
handling here.

Mermaid puts classDef classes on the g.node wrapper, and the default mermaid
sheet paints nodes with !important too, so these selectors target g.activeStyle
descendants to win the cascade on either shape.

This sheet is text/css: TW's wikitext stylesheet parser rewrites the
--lithic-c-* double hyphens into en-dashes inside text/vnd.tiddlywiki sheets.
*/

/* Active node fill/border = accent pair (accent-fg is derived >= 4.5:1 on accent) */
div.mm-themed:not(.mm-user) g.activeStyle rect,
div.mm-themed:not(.mm-user) g.activeStyle .basic.label-container,
div.mm-themed:not(.mm-user) rect.activeStyle,
div.mm-themed:not(.mm-user) .activeStyle rect {
    fill: var(--lithic-c-accent) !important;
    stroke: var(--lithic-c-accent-fg) !important;
    stroke-width: 2px !important;
}

/* Active node label keeps the derived accent foreground in all label shapes */
div.mm-themed:not(.mm-user) g.activeStyle text,
div.mm-themed:not(.mm-user) g.activeStyle .label div span,
div.mm-themed:not(.mm-user) g.activeStyle .label div p,
div.mm-themed:not(.mm-user) g.activeStyle span.nodeLabel p,
div.mm-themed:not(.mm-user) text.activeStyle {
    fill: var(--lithic-c-accent-fg) !important;
    color: var(--lithic-c-accent-fg) !important;
    font-weight: bold !important;
}